0095:                   * 05/25/93 mod - Boisy Pitre's non-sharable device patches
0095:                   * 01/15/10 mod - Boisy Pitre redoes his non-sharable device patch
0095: 2713                       beq   Yespath      No paths open, so we know we can open it
0097:                   * IOMan has already vetted the mode byte of the driver and the descriptor
0097:                   * and compared it to REGA of I$Open (now in PD.MOD of this current path).
0097:                   * here we know there is at least one path open for this device.
0097:                   * in order to properly support SHARE. (device exclusivity), we get the
0097:                   * mode byte for the path we are opening and see if the SHARE. bit is set.
0097:                   * if so, then we return error since we cannot have exclusivity to the device.
0097:                            IFNE  H6309
0097:                            tim   #SHARE.,PD.MOD,y
0097:                            ELSE
0097: A621                       lda   PD.MOD,y 
0099: 8540                       bita  #SHARE.
009B:                            ENDC
009B: 2606                       bne   NoShare      
009D:                   * we now know that the path's mode doesn't have the SHARE. bit set, so 
009D:                   * we need to look at the mode of the path in the list header pointer to
009D:                   * see if ITS SHARE. bit is set (meaning it wants exclusive access to the
009D:                   * port).  If so we bail out
009D:                            IFNE  H6309
009D:                            tim   #SHARE.,PD.MOD,x
009D:                            ELSE
009D: A601                       lda   PD.MOD,x 
009F: 8540                       bita  #SHARE.
00A1:                            ENDC
