06DD:                   ********************************************************************
06DD:                   * KANJI extension (Japanese text editing in ReadLn)
06DD:                   *
06DD:                   * The path descriptor option PD.PAR (unused by the SCF drivers of the
06DD:                   * simulator) selects the character encoding of the terminal:
06DD:                   *   0 = single byte (original behaviour)   1 = UTF-8
06DD:                   *   2 = EUC-JP                             3 = Shift_JIS (CP932)
06DD:                   * In these modes a backspace removes one whole character from the line
06DD:                   * buffer and the erase sequence (BSE or BSE,SP,BSE) is echoed once for
06DD:                   * every display column the character occupies (2 for full width kanji
06DD:                   * and kana, 1 for ASCII and half width katakana).
06DD:                   *
06DD:                   * Entry: X = character count (> 0), U = buffer pointer, Y = path descriptor
06DD:                   * Exit : X, U moved back over the last character
06DD: 3084              KBsp     leax  ,x           Any characters?
06DF: 1027FFB4                   lbeq  L03A2        No, return
06E3: 3450                       pshs  x,u          S: X(0) U(2)
06E5: AE28                       ldx   PD.BUF,y     start of the line buffer
06E7: 3410                       pshs  x            S: last(0) X(2) U(4)
06E9: AC64              KB.scan  cmpx  4,s          reached the end of the line?
06EB: 2407                       bhs   KB.end       yes
06ED: AFE4                       stx   ,s           remember start of this character
06EF: 8D45                       bsr   KB.len       B = length of the character at ,X
06F1: 3A                         abx                skip it
06F2: 20F5                       bra   KB.scan
